Description: add a udev-backed USB device enumeration layer
 The legacy USB kit (USBKit.h: BUSBDevice, BUSBConfiguration,
 BUSBInterface, BUSBEndpoint, BUSBRoster) has no V\OS counterpart, and
 there is no device add-on interface to replace it with. Provide the
 subset this app uses, backed by udev (enumerate + hotplug monitor) and
 the device filesystem:
 .
  - device strings, ids, class fields come from /sys/bus/usb/devices;
  - interfaces and endpoints are read from the sysfs entries named
    "<device>:<config>.<interface>" and their ep_* directories;
  - only the active configuration is exposed (the device filesystem
    keeps descriptors for that one), and class-specific raw descriptors
    report B_ERROR, so the info window lists none;
  - roster devices are owned by the roster and kept alive through
    Stop(), so removal messages already in flight stay matchable.
Author: Dario Casalinuovo <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- /dev/null
+++ b/USBKit.h
@@ -0,0 +1,166 @@
+/*
